<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajmala</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rajmala chronicle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rajmala is a chronicle of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a>, written in Bengali verse. Its first part is traditionally dated to the 15th century, in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharma">Dharma</a> Manikya I, and later sections continued it into the modern period. It traces the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikya-dynasty">Manikya dynasty</a> through a long legendary line back to the lunar dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> myth, and it remains the main narrative source for the history of the kingdom.</p></div>
